\f0\b\fs32 \cf3 9. Relationship to LEARNING_SYSTEM.docx
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 This document is a companion to LEARNING_SYSTEM.docx, not a replacement for any of its sections. The relationship is exclusive at the per-skill level \'97 a given skill, at a given moment, is either being taught through the Score Loop or being taught through the Stuck protocol, never both. Several cross-references matter for the operational team:
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f5\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 3 (Score Loop). 
\f4\i0\b0 The default loop the Stuck protocol replaces when triggered. Frame \uc0\u8594  Attempt \u8594  Score+Diagnose \u8594  Repair remains the architecture for any skill not currently in Stuck protocol.\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f5\i\b \ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 4 (Repair Modes). The intra-loop escalation from Tighten to Show on confidence drop is the prerequisite condition for entering the Stuck protocol. If that escalation has not been allowed to run, the loop has not actually failed yet \'97 re-attempts of Tighten or Show should precede Stuck-protocol entry.\
\ls5\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 5 (Lock). Spaced retrieval continues to be the engine. The Stuck protocol interacts with the Lock as detailed in Section 6 of this document \'97 modifying intervals and surface-form selection but not replacing the underlying queue.\
\ls5\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 11 (Out of Scope). This document is the natural companion named there. With this document committed, the Stuck Student protocol moves out of Section 11 of LEARNING_SYSTEM in the next minor version of that doc, and the cross-reference here replaces it.\
\ls5\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 13 (Data and Improvement). The same data posture applies. Student response data captured during Stuck protocol attempts is treated under the same rules as Score Loop data. Aggregate, anonymized signals about move effectiveness can inform editorial content review (Section 6.4 of this document).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb360\sa180\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs32 \cf3 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 10. Out of Scope for This Document
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f5\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Human escalation. The decision to keep the Stuck protocol AI-only is locked. If a future product decision introduces human tutors, parent escalation, or teacher handoff, that mechanism belongs in a separate document and should not be retrofit into this protocol.\
\ls6\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Content authoring for Stuck-protocol artifacts. Step Sideways requires authored contrasting cases. Step Apart requires authored sub-skill decompositions. Step Down requires authored prerequisite-skill content with its own mini-Score-Loops. The authoring workflow for these belongs in CONTENT_AUTHORING.docx (forthcoming) and is out of scope here.\
\ls6\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Diagnostic-driven move selection. An earlier design considered a diagnostic step at protocol entry that would infer the cause of stuckness and pick the move accordingly. That approach is explicitly rejected in favor of the Sideways-first plus student-choice sequence. The rejected design and the reasons for rejecting it are noted here only to prevent re-litigation.\
\ls6\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Detection of off-task or low-effort responses inside the Stuck protocol. The effort and coaching signals in LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 10.5 continue to apply; their integration with Stuck-protocol-specific telemetry is out of scope here.\
\ls6\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Efficacy measurement. How Cramapple measures whether the Stuck protocol is working \'97 resolution rates by move, by skill, by subject \'97 is part of the broader efficacy-measurement workstream that is out of scope across all teaching documents and owned by analytics.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb360\sa180\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs32 \cf3 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 11. Open Items
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0
\f5\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Exact threshold for \'93persistently low diagnostic confidence\'94 as an entry trigger. Working assumption: two consecutive attempts where the highest-confidence error classification falls below 0.6. Requires calibration on real student data.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Whether stuck-resolved skills should Lock at a shorter interval than standard (24 hours instead of 24\'9672 hours) to account for fragility of hard-won resolution. Working assumption: same interval; revisit if re-loss rates run higher than baseline.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Number of Park re-emergence cycles before editorial intervention. Working assumption: two parks on the same skill for the same student triggers content-team review.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Thresholds for preference memory activation. Working assumption: three choice-prompt encounters, 2-of-3 consistency, 50% resolution rate. All three numbers require calibration.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Visual treatment of the choice prompt buttons relative to MCQ buttons. Working assumption: contained block, subtle background color shift, positioned below the question region. UX details deferred to the broader design system pass.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Whether the parent-facing effort rollup surfaces parked-skill counts at all, or only aggregate effort. Tied to the parent-incentive-mechanism open item in LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 12.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 How to handle the case where a Step Down prerequisite is itself a skill the student has been parked on. Working assumption: surface a second-order prerequisite if one exists; otherwise the system parks the original skill immediately without running Step Down and surfaces both for editorial review. Edge case but real.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Whether the alternate-move suggestion in Section 4.4 (after the first student-chosen move fails) should be surfaced as a button or as a system message. Working assumption: system message with an inline accept/decline; lighter than a full second choice prompt.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Whether to expose the preference memory to the student in any form (e.g., \'93you usually find it helpful to see the foundation first\'97want to start there?\'94). Working assumption: no, the bias is invisible. Worth testing whether surfacing it adds metacognitive value or feels like surveillance.\
\ls7\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Whether the Stuck protocol should ever fire on student-supplied questions (LEARNING_SYSTEM Section 8) or only on canonical-portfolio questions. Working assumption: canonical only at launch; student-supplied questions Park immediately on persistent miss without running the full protocol, because the prerequisite-skill graph required for Step Down does not exist for non-canonical content.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb360\sa180\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs32 \cf3 \ulnone \strike0\striked0 12. Operating Implications
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa120\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs22 \cf3 Several downstream artifacts need updates once this document is committed.
\f1\fs24 \cf0 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f5\i\b\fs22 \cf3 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 LEARNING_SYSTEM.docx. Section 11 (Out of Scope) loses the first bullet \'97 the Stuck Student protocol is no longer out of scope. Section 11 renumbering of subsequent items downstream is not required; only the bullet is removed. A cross-reference to this document is added at Sections 3.5 (Lock), 4.4 (Selection Logic), and 5.1 (Lock spacing) so that the operational team can navigate between the two documents fluently.\
\ls8\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 PEDAGOGY.docx. The Driver/Chi conceptual-change citations, Sweller cognitive load citations, Bloom/VanLehn mastery learning citations, Kapur productive-failure citations, and Cronbach/Snow aptitude-treatment-interaction citations should be present in PEDAGOGY. Any that are missing should be added in the next minor version.\
\ls8\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Content authoring. Orly and the hired experts need a content backlog: contrasting cases for Step Sideways across the FRQ archetypes; sub-skill decompositions for Step Apart on the quantitative and procedural skills most likely to overload working memory; prerequisite-skill mini-loops for the highest-failure-rate skills identified in pilot data. This is the largest operating cost of the Stuck protocol and the largest dependency for launch readiness.\
\ls8\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 ECONOMICS.docx. Inference-cost model needs an update. The Stuck protocol is more expensive per skill than the Score Loop \'97 up to three additional teaching cycles on a single skill. Marginal cost per stuck-skill event needs estimation; aggregate impact on inference cost depends on the rate at which skills enter the Stuck protocol, which is itself an open empirical question.\
\ls8\ilvl0\ulnone \strike0\striked0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\ul \strike \strikec3 Engineering. The skill-state machine needs a Stuck mode with the Sub-states Sideways, ChoicePrompt, Apart, Down, OfferAlternate, and Parked. The Lock needs preference-memory storage per student. The button-based choice prompt is a new UX primitive that must be added to the component library.\
